{
  "comment": [
    "Firestore creates single-field indexes on its own, for one collection at",
    "a time, and rejects composite entries that declare one — so a query",
    "ordered by a single field needs no entry in indexes. The exception is a",
    "query across every collection of one name (a collection group): those",
    "need the field turned on for that scope in fieldOverrides, where the",
    "three collection-scope defaults have to be restated or they are dropped."
  ],
